  "query_preview": "Small Craft Advisory for the western waters until 01z,\nbut expect some areas will see wind speeds drop off below Small\nCraft Advisory just before then. Where Gale Warnings are\ncurrently in effect, I issued a Small Craft Advisory until 03z.\nWinds and waves are expected to fall off pretty quickly there\nthis evening as well as high pressure moves in from the west\novernight. Winds will become light tonight, then south to\nsouthwesterly Thursday. There may be some gusts in the 20-25 kt\nrange up near Grand Portage Thursday afternoon, but otherwise\nexpect gusts below 20 kt. Gusty southwest winds are expected on\nFriday with showers and thunderstorms during the afternoon and\nevening. Some strong to severe storms capable of strong winds to\naround 40 kt and large hail are possible. Gusty winds persist\nthrough Saturday with a wind shift to west-northwesterly through\nthe day. Monday and Tuesday will be the next chance for\nhazardous marine conditions. Gales are possible (60% chance),\nespecially along the North Shore, on Monday.\n\nFor the open water discussion, refer to the NWS Marquette Area \nForecast Discussion at weather.gov/mqt.",
